# Stow's global ignore list. stow(8) reads this from ~/.stow-global-ignore;
# the bash package stows it there — upstream designed the file to be managed
# by stow itself (see the note in Stow.pm's get_ignore_regexps()).
#
# When this file exists it REPLACES stow's built-in defaults, so those
# defaults are reproduced verbatim below (extracted from stow 2.4.1,
# /usr/share/perl5/vendor_perl/Stow.pm, __DATA__ block) ahead of our
# additions.
#
# Semantics, from the same source: each pattern is a Perl regex. A pattern
# containing a slash is matched against the path relative to the package top
# (prefixed with "/"), anchored at segment boundaries; a pattern without a
# slash is matched fully anchored against the basename, at any depth. Note a
# .stow-local-ignore inside a package would REPLACE this file for that
# package — don't add one without reproducing these patterns.

RCS
.+,v

CVS
\.\#.+       # CVS conflict files / emacs lock files
\.cvsignore

\.svn
_darcs
\.hg

\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules

.+~          # emacs backup files
\#.*\#       # emacs autosave files

^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING

# --- Additions (2026-08-26, context-policy Stage 2) --------------------------
# Per-package charters are agent documentation, never to be symlinked into
# live config dirs — a stray ~/CLAUDE.md stowed from the bash package would
# load into every Claude session under $HOME.
CLAUDE\.md
